152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (IS A HIGH-ALTITUDECOLD DESERT LOCATED IN THE NORTHEASTERN REGION OFHIMACHAL PRADESH, CLOSETO THE INDO-TIBETAN BORDER. SURROUNDED BY DRAMATIC MOUNTAINS AND DEEP VALLEYS CARVED BYTHE SPITI RIVER, SPITI IS RENOWNED FOR ITS ANCIENT BUDDHIST MONASTERIES SUCH AS KEY, DHANKAR, AND TABO, WHICH REFLECT CENTURIES-OLD TIBETAN BUDDHIST TRADITIONS AND SPIRITUAL LIFE. THE LOCAL CULTURE IS SIMPLE AND RESILIENT, WITH PRAYER FLAGS, MONASTERIES, AND CLOSE-KNIT VILLAGES FORMING THE HEART OF EVERYDAY LIFE. A JOURNEY TO SPITI OFFERS TRAVELERS A RARE BLEND OF BREATHTAKING LANDSCAPES, SPIRITUALITY, AND AN AUTHENTIC HIMALAYAN WAY OF LIVING.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
